# One coverage test per backend, driven by doc/capabilities.json: every keyed
# cell of the backend (support/timing_coverage.hpp: macs, key derivations and
# password hashes, one per hmac a cell lists, and BLAKE2b with a key, the
# blake3 type's keyed modes and bcrypt_verify) enters its own
# detail::timing_guard first; every digest cell without a key, and every
# Boost.Hash2-form type, enters none. A new cell of a family the support
# knows gets its call from backend_has_v, which capabilities keeps equal to the
# table; a cell of a family or function it does not know fails until its call
# is written. backends::webcrypto has none (design D6).
